canon includes third-party data.

Versification schemes
  data/schemes/{org,eng,lxx,vul,rsc,rso}.json, and the tables generated from
  them (src/scheme_tables.rs, ts/scheme-tables.ts).

  From the Copenhagen Alliance versification mappings,
  https://github.com/nida-institute/versification
  (versification-mappings/standard-mappings/, commit 519af776ab65d89a51e37f750779250f940459ef).
  Created by Neil Rees, Reinier de Blois, Mike Lothers, Tim Steenwyk,
  Peter Kirk and Matjaž Crnivec, from Paratext's VRS files.

  Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
  (CC BY-SA 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/.
  The files are unchanged. The generated tables keep their chapter and verse
  counts, exclusions and verse mappings; drop six Paratext-only book codes
  (BLT, DNT, JDB, JSA, SST, TBS) and org.json's own mappings; and correct
  four mapping rows that are evident typos (listed in gen-canon's ERRATA and
  data/schemes/README.md). Those tables are a CC BY-SA 4.0 adaptation.

Sniffing rules
  data/sniff/rules.json, and the table generated from it (src/sniff_tables.rs).

  nida-institute/versification's versification-sniffing/rules/merged_rules.json
  (commit 519af776ab65d89a51e37f750779250f940459ef), CC BY-SA 4.0 as above,
  derived from TVTMS: STEPBible's Translators' Versification Traditions with
  Methodology for Standardisation, Tyndale House, Cambridge
  (https://github.com/STEPBible/STEPBible-Data), CC BY 4.0. The file is
  unchanged; the generated table keeps the tests and column labels, adds which
  columns each built-in scheme fits, and drops the ranges.

Ours
  data/schemes/ulb.json is ours: chapter and verse counts measured from
  WycliffeAssociates/en_ulb, with eng.json's verse mappings for the 66 books
  copied in. Because it carries those mappings it is also CC BY-SA 4.0.
